import theorem            proofs/wiedijk/sum-formula/sum-formula
import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-extended
import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-single

theorem square-of-sum-equals-sum-of-cubes
  note        The sum of the first n numbers is n(n + 1)/2. By induction on n,
              the sum of the first n cubes is the square of that: adding
              (k + 1)³ to (k(k + 1)/2)² gives ((k + 1)(k + 2)/2)².
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then (Σ(k = 1 to n) k)² = Σ(k = 1 to n) k³

let C(m) = Σ(j = 1 to m) j³, for m ∈ ℕ                                (D1)
       reads the sum of the first m cubes

1.  For all k ∈ ℕ, C(k) = (k(k + 1)/2)².
    induction on k starting at 1

    base
    1.1.  Σ(j = 1 to 1) j³ = 1³
          mun:sum-single a := 1

    1.2.  C(1) = (1(1 + 1)/2)²
          calculation
            C(1) = Σ(j = 1 to 1) j³     D1
                 = 1³                   1.1
                 = (1(1 + 1)/2)²        arithmetic

    step
    let k ∈ ℕ                                                         (K)
    assume step 1 is true for k, the induction hypothesis             (IH)

    1.3.  Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j³ = Σ(j = 1 to k) j³ + (k + 1)³
          mun:sum-extended a := 1, n := k
          requires k ≥ 1: from K

    1.4.  C(k + 1) = C(k) + (k + 1)³
          calculation
            C(k + 1) = Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j³          D1
                     = Σ(j = 1 to k) j³ + (k + 1)³   1.3
                     = C(k) + (k + 1)³               D1

    1.5.  C(k) + (k + 1)³ = (k(k + 1)/2)² + (k + 1)³
          substitute C(k) = (k(k + 1)/2)² (IH)

    1.6.  (k(k + 1)/2)² + (k + 1)³ = ((k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2)²
          algebra

    1.7.  C(k + 1) = ((k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2)²
          calculation
            C(k + 1) = C(k) + (k + 1)³                     1.4
                     = (k(k + 1)/2)² + (k + 1)³            1.5
                     = ((k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2)²           1.6

2.  C(n) = (n(n + 1)/2)²
    instantiate k := n in line 1

3.  Σ(k = 1 to n) k = n(n + 1)/2
    thm:sum-formula

4.  (Σ(k = 1 to n) k)² = (n(n + 1)/2)²
    substitute Σ(k = 1 to n) k = n(n + 1)/2 (line 3)

5.  (Σ(k = 1 to n) k)² = Σ(k = 1 to n) k³
    calculation
      (Σ(k = 1 to n) k)² = (n(n + 1)/2)²      4
                         = C(n)               2
                         = Σ(k = 1 to n) k³   D1
